=== text ===
The sky appears blue because of a phenomenon called **Rayleigh scattering**. When sunlight (which contains all colors of the visible spectrum) passes through the Earth's atmosphere, it interacts with gas molecules like nitrogen and nitrogen.

Shorter wavelengths of light—such as blue and violet—scatter much more strongly than longer wavelengths due to their shorter wavelengths. Since the human eye is more sensitive to blue light than red, our eyes perceive the sky as blue. The shorter the wavelength of the light, the more it is scattered, which is why the sky appears blue during the day.
