=== text ===
The sky appears blue because sunlight, which is made of all colors of the visible spectrum, interacts with Earth's atmosphere in a way that depends on wavelength. As sunlight travels through the atmosphere, molecules like nitrogen and nitrogen dioxide scatter shorter wavelengths (blue light) much more strongly than longer wavelengths such as red or yellow. This scattering phenomenon, known as Rayleigh scattering, scatters blue light from all directions, making the sky appear blue to our eyes, while allowing most of the longer-wavelength red light to pass through relatively unimpeded when looking directly at the sun.
