=== text ===
The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called **Rayleigh scattering**, which occurs when sunlight interacts with the molecules in Earth's atmosphere. Sunlight consists of all colors of the visible spectrum, but different wavelengths are scattered differently depending on their wavelength: shorter wavelengths (blue and violet light) scatter much more strongly than longer-wavelength red or yellow light. While Rayleigh scattering affects all wavelengths to some degree, its effect is inversely proportional to the fourth power of the wavelength ($\lambda^{-4}$), meaning blue light—being at a shorter wavelength—is scattered much more intensely than red light. This phenomenon not only scatters sunlight into our eyes from every direction (making the sky appear blue) but also creates the vivid blue skies we observe on clear days, while allowing us to see clearly against the sunless background of space.
