=== text ===
The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called **Rayleigh scattering**, which occurs when sunlight interacts with the molecules in Earth's atmosphere. Sunlight consists of all colors visible on the electromagnetic spectrum, but each color travels at slightly different speeds through air molecules because they interact differently depending on their wavelength (wavelengths).

Sunlight is made up of various wavelengths of light; red has longer waves and less energy, while violet/blue/violet light scatters much more strongly. When sunlight enters Earth's atmosphere, gas molecules scatter the shorter blue wavelengths far more effectively than other colors because these shorter wavelengths are scattered in all directions by atmospheric particles (a phenomenon known as Rayleigh scattering), making our sky appear blue during the day and sunrises/sunsets when those rays travel through thicker layers of air.
